"Ask Raleigh - Identify, Request, Resolve | Raleighnc.gov (https://raleighnc.gov/ask-raleigh-fix-report-request/services/ask-raleigh-identify-request-resolve)\nciteturn4view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn3view0\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 63\nL0: Menu\nL1: \nL2: [Input] [Button: Search]\nL3: \nL4: 【0†Image: Raleighnc.gov logo】\nL5: Thank you for printing this page from the City of Raleigh's Official Website (www.raleighnc.gov)\nL6: https://raleighnc.gov/ask-raleigh-fix-report-request/services/ask-raleigh-identify-request-resolve\nL7: 10/20/2026 12:12 pm\nL8: # Ask Raleigh - Identify, Request, Resolve\nL9: \nL10: Customer Experience Center - Your New Way to Connect with the City\nL11: \nL12: Updated: Oct 20, 2026\nL13: \nL14: 【1†Visit the Ask Raleigh portal now!†ask.raleighnc.gov】\nL15: \nL16: The City of Raleigh is excited to introduce Ask Raleigh, a new online portal that makes it easier than ever for residents to request services, report issues, and get help from the City.  Ask Raleigh is more than just a tech upgrade - it’s the first step in a bold, citywide strategy to reimagine customer service.\nL17: Replacing the current SeeClickFix tool, Ask Raleigh is designed to be faster, smarter, and more intuitive, helping residents get what they need while supporting a more unified response across City departments.\nL18: \nL19: Why you’ll love Ask Raleigh:\nL20:   * Track requests in real time – Get updates on your request and see progress as it happens;\nL21:   * Avoid duplicate reports – Already reported? Ask Raleigh will let you know;\nL22:   * Smarter service – The tool alerts you if the issue is outside City limits, so nothing gets lost or misdirected; and,\nL23:   * Easier to use – Enhanced maps and a simplified interface make reporting quick and clear.\nL24:   * Ask Raleigh is also the first step in the City’s new Customer Experience strategy—a forward-thinking initiative that will expand even further when the new City Hall opens in 2027. This launch lays the foundation for a more connected, responsive City where every department plays a role in delivering excellent service.\nL25: Ask Raleigh will keep evolving based on what you tell us.\nL26: \nL27: 【2†iframe†ral.maps.arcgis.com】\nL28: ## Contact\nL29: \nL30: \nL31: \nL32: Customer Experience Management Team\nL33: CustomerService@raleighnc.gov\nL34: ## Subscribe\nL35: \nL36: \nL37: \nL38: [Input] [Input] Enter your email to view all topics [Input: email@address.com] [Input]\nL39: \nL40: Lead Department:\nL41:     【3†City Manager's Office】\nL42: \nL43: Was this page helpful?\nL44: \nL45: [Input] Yes\nL46: \nL47: [Input] No\nL48: \nL49: Email [Input]\nL50: \nL51: Please choose the type of issue you are experiencing with the page from the dropdown. [Select]\nL52: \nL53: Comments\nL54: \nL55: [Input] Would you like to be notified by the City about your feedback?\nL56: \nL57: This feedback widget is not intended for customer service issues.\nL58: This feedback is reviewed monthly to help us improve our site. For immediate customer service please refer to our 【4†staff directory】.\nL59: \nL60: [Input]\nL61: \nL62: [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input]\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEvents | Raleighnc.gov (https://raleighnc.gov/events/calendar)\nciteturn4view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn3view1\",\"lineno\":0}); Total lines: 272\nL0: Menu\nL1: \nL2: [Input] [Button: Search]\nL3: \nL4: Alert\nL5: \nL6: ## 【0†City Offices Closed Nov. 11】\nL7: \nL8: City offices are closed Wednesday, Nov. 11 in observance of Veterans Day.\nL9: \nL10: Published 11/6/2026 at 7 a.m. Updated 11/6/2026 at 10 a.m.\nL11: \nL12: # Events\nL13: \nL14:   * 【1†List View】\nL15:   * 【2†Calendar View】\nL16: \nL17: Department [Select]\nL18: \nL19: Core Service [Select]\nL20: \nL21: Event Type [Select]\nL22: \nL23: [Input]